.TH HELIOS 1 "2026" "helios" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
helios \- desktop for Claude Code, OpenAI Codex and OpenRouter coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B helios
.SH DESCRIPTION
Helios is a native GTK4/libadwaita desktop that keeps every coding-agent
session in one window: what the agent is doing, what it may do, and what it
has spent. Claude sessions drive the official
.B claude
CLI, GPT sessions bind to a persistent Codex App Server, and OpenRouter
sessions run Helios's own agent loop. Install and sign in to the CLIs
separately; Helios finds
.B claude
via
.B $HELIOS_CLAUDE_BINARY
, then PATH, then its standalone install locations.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HELIOS_CLAUDE_BINARY
Path of the claude binary to use instead of the one on PATH.
.TP
.B HELIOS_CODEX_BINARY
Path of the codex binary to use instead of the one on PATH.
.TP
.B HELIOS_DEBUG
Set to 1 for wire-level driver tracing.
.TP
.B HELIOS_LOG_LEVEL
Python logging level; WARNING quiets the default INFO.
.TP
.B HELIOS_STATE_DIR
Root for the log, the Work database, per-conversation permissions,
checkpoints, goals and OpenRouter session history (default ~/.helios).
ui-state.json, openrouter.key, the caches, backups/ and session-archive/
stay under ~/.helios regardless; override HOME to relocate everything.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.helios/
Works, goals, UI state and editor backups.
.TP
.I ~/.claude/projects/
Claude Code transcripts, read for sessions and status.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/spencercnorton/helios
